<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 15 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 15 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp Financial Security Assurance on Tuesday said it qualified for bond insurance the following 15 issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Anaheim, Calif, $95 million Electricity Revs.</p>
<p>--California State University, $13.13 million Revs.</p>
<p>--California State University, $4 million Revs.</p>
<p>--Tinley Park, Ill., $3.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Westford, Mass., $9.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Mount Pleasant, Mich., $1.885 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Becker, Minn., $5.35 million GOs refunding.</p>
<p>--Leonia Board of Education, N.J., $4.99 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Clark County, Nev., $120 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Ohio State Public Facilities Higher Education, $150 million.</p>
<p>--Ohio State Public Facilities Mental Health, $40 million.</p>
<p>--Beaverton S.D., Ore., $16.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Beaverton S.D., Ore., $22 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Williamsport Area S.D., Penn., $5.47 million GOs</p>
<p>--Cumberland County S.D., Wis., $8.5 million refunding GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
